at \\(1010101 + 989899 = 2000000\\) and \\(989899 + 1010101 = 2000000\\). So the expression simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n= 1001001 \\cdot 2000000 - 1001 \\cdot 2000000\n\\]\n\nWe can factor out the common factor \\(2000000\\):\n\n\\[\n= 2000000(1001001 - 1001)\n\\]\n\nSimplify inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\n= 2000000(1000000)\n\\]\n\nNow, we multiply the terms:\n\n\\[\n= 2000000 \\cdot 1000000 = 2000000000000\n\\]\n\nThe number \\(2000000000000\\) has the rightmost non-zero digit as \\(2\\) and is followed by \\(12\\) zeroes. Therefore, the ordered pair \\((a, b)\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{(2, 12)}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{(2, 12)}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
